text:
amanda: Quick sync — AcmeHealth POC. They want streaming SSE + function/tool calls + strict structured JSON output for downstream ingestion. Also asked about SSO/KMS for Private deployment and committed QPS pricing. Any obvious blockers?

raj: We can do streaming + fn calls. Main presales items: 1) ephemeral creds for the adapter, 2) schema enforcement on the response, 3) fallback model for cold starts. For SSO/KMS we need their IdP metadata and KMS provider (AWS KMS or GCP KMS).

leo: Pricing note: committed QPS for Dedicated reduces unit cost ~30% at our standard bands. Need expected peak & 99th latency SLO to size. If they want private on prem we'll need a support ticket for install window (2-3 weeks).

amanda: They asked whether we support a single websocket connection multiplexing multiple sessions — and how tool calls look in streaming. Can you paste a tiny SDK snippet for them to try?

raj: Yup. Example (node):

```js
// simple SSE + function call example
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = client.stream({ model: 'redwood-2-stream' });
stream.on('data', chunk => { console.log('tok', chunk.token); });
// tool call arrives as structured event
stream.on('tool_call', evt => {
  // evt = { name: 'lookup_patient', args: { id: '123' } }
  // caller should return JSON stringified result to continue generation
});
```

raj: For structured outputs we recommend validating the model output against a JSON schema in the app. We also provide an optional "schema_hints" prompt parameter to reduce validation failures.

olivia: Security questionnaire bits: they asked about data residency (EU), audit logs, and KMS key rotation. We can offer VPC Private deployment in EU region + audit retention addon. KMS is customer-managed; rotation follows their KMS policy.

amanda: Great. They've got one blocker: legal wants to see L3 network diagram and proof of no persistent storage for ephemeral sessions. Where do I grab a diagram?

leo: I have a network diagram for Dedicated + Private; pulling now. For ephemeral sessions: runtime keeps KV cache in-memory only; no token logs written to disk by default. We do persist aggregated usage metrics to analytics (anonymized). I can paste the short blurb for legal.

raj: Also note: for streaming with tool calls, if you want guaranteed ordering and exactly-once semantics you'll want to run via Dedicated with sticky sessions; otherwise our hosted tier may route across pods and tool call handlers must be idempotent.

amanda: Can you two draft the legal blurb and a short runbook for the POC engineer (handshake steps, ephemeral creds rotation, sample curl + handshake flow)? They want that before demo tomorrow afternoon.

deploy-bot: Deploy succeeded: acmehealth/poc-dedicated-v2 at commit abc123 — region: eu-west-1 :rocket:

raj: Drafted runbook below (short):
1) Exchange IdP metadata and KMS ARN with us.
2) We provision a test Dedicated pool (EU) and enable ephemeral role for the adapter.
3) Customer runs a short handshake: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/handshake -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" -d '{"session_id":"test-123"}'` — SDK will return a websocket URL.
4) Client opens SSE/ws, sends initial schema hint: `\{"schema_hints\": { ... } }`.
5) On tool_call events, call the adapter webhook and respond with JSON string.
6) After demo, rotate ephemeral creds (we'll provide rotation endpoint).

leo: Legal blurb for ephemeral sessions: \"Runtime stores transient KV caches in-memory for the duration of model inference only; no user prompt or response tokens are written to persistent storage in our Dedicated or Private offerings unless客户 enables logging. Aggregated, anonymized usage metrics and telemetry are retained per contract. We support customer-managed KMS for encryption at rest and provide audit logs for admin events.\"

amanda: Perfect. Last: can we give them an estimated weekly cost for a 500 QPS sustained test for 1 week on Dedicated (EU)? Even a ballpark.

leo: Ballpark: 500 QPS sustained -> ~43M tokens/day (depends on prompt/response). For Dedicated test the one-week reserved pool + support & EU infra — rough estimate 28k–45k USD for the week including support. If they do commit monthly it drops significantly. I'll follow up with formal quote.

amanda: Thanks all — I'll send this to the customer and attach the network diagram + runbook. Ping me if you want me to redline the legal blurb. :thumbsup:
